## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates testing approaches for real-time ML moderation systems with canary deployments, privacy requirements, and drift detection capabilities—extending beyond basic functional testing.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end latency and throughput optimization
- Data privacy and PII masking protocols
- Canary deployment strategies with automated rollback
- Model drift detection and monitoring systems
- Contract testing between microservices and components

## Code Example
```javascript
// Latency contract validation (pseudo-code)
async function validateLatencyContract(moderationRequest) {
  const startTime = Date.now();
  const result = await moderationService.process(moderationRequest);
  const latency = Date.now() - startTime;

  if (latency > 200) {
    throw new Error(`SLA breach: ${latency}ms > 200ms`);
  }

  return { result, latency };
}

// Drift detection monitoring
function detectModelDrift(currentMetrics, baselineMetrics) {
  const precisionDrift = Math.abs(currentMetrics.precision - baselineMetrics.precision);
  const recallDrift = Math.abs(currentMetrics.recall - baselineMetrics.recall);

  return precisionDrift > 0.05 || recallDrift > 0.05;
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates candidates' practical testing strategies for edge, multi-region policy engines with hot updates. The focus is on correctness, tenant isolation, and safe rollouts under adverse conditions.

## Key Concepts

- **Edge-path correctness** versus centralized policy evaluation
- **Tenant isolation** and data-plane versus control-plane divergence
- **Canary rollouts**, versioning, and rollback criteria
- **Chaos testing**, update latency, and policy auditing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-policy evaluation hook
function evalEdgePolicy(request, tenantId, edgeRules, centralRules) {
  const edgeDecision = evaluateRules(request, edgeRules[tenantId]);
  const centralDecision = evaluateRules(request, centralRules[tenantId]);

  if (edgeDecision !== centralDecision) {
    logConsistencyViolation(tenantId, edgeDecision, centralDecision);
    return { decision: centralDecision, divergence: true };
  }

  return { decision: edgeDecision, divergence: false };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design end-to-end, fault-tolerant data pipelines and reason about exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics in real-time systems.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end testing of streaming pipelines
- Idempotency and deduplication strategies
- Replay, backpressure, and regional outage resilience
- Metrics: data loss, duplicates, latency, SLAs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple dedup: track seen event_ids to skip duplicates in sinks
const seen = new Set();
function process(event){
  if(seen.has(event.event_id)) return false; // duplicate
  seen.add(event.event_id);
  // write to sink
  return true;
}
```

